#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Declare dependencies {#declare-dependencies}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A managed workflow runs in a Python environment that it prepares in advance."
" The job cannot reach the internet, so it cannot `pip install` packages. "
"Instead, Qiskit and a list of [supported packages](#check-which-packages-"
"are-installed) are already installed, and you can [upload wheels](#add-your-"
"own-packages) for any other package that your workflow needs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Check which packages are installed {#check-which-packages-are-installed}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every job runs with Python 3.12 on Linux (x86_64), with the following "
"packages installed:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`qiskit`, `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, `qiskit-serverless`, and their dependencies,"
" such as `numpy`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The supported packages, such as `qiskit-aer`, `qiskit-addon-sqd`, `qiskit-"
"addon-utils`, `qiskit-mitigation`, `qiskit-addon-slc`, `qiskit-paulice`, "
"`ffsim`, and `pyscf`. Each is installed at one fixed version.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To see the supported packages and their versions, call "
"`dependencies_versions()` from your local notebook:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: dependencies_versions() lists only requirements-dynamic-dependencies.txt. It omits qiskit, qiskit-ibm-runtime, qiskit-serverless, and numpy, although they are installed. */}\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Your workflow can import any of these packages without setup. The workflow "
"installs them when it builds the environment, not when a job starts, so they"
" do not add to the start time of a job.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A workflow does not read a `requirements.txt` or `pyproject.toml` file, so "
"it does not install the packages that these files list. The `dependencies` "
"argument of `ManagedWorkflow` is deprecated and ignored, so it does not "
"install packages either. Remove it from your upload code, and [upload "
"wheels](#add-your-own-packages) instead.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Packages on GPU compute profiles {#packages-on-gpu-compute-profiles}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Jobs that run on a [GPU compute profile](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-"
"profiles) also have the following CUDA packages installed. These packages "
"work only on a GPU profile, and `dependencies_versions()` does not list "
"them. Do not upload your own CUDA wheels, because they conflict with these "
"versions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Package | Version |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `gpu4pyscf-cuda12x` | 1.8.1 |\n"
"| `gpu4pyscf-libxc-cuda12x` | 0.8.1 |\n"
"| `cupy-cuda12x` | 14.2.0 |\n"
"| `cutensor-cu12` | 2.8.0 |\n"
"| `cuda-pathfinder` | 1.8.5 |\n"
"| `nvidia-cublas-cu12` | 12.9.3.13 |\n"
"| `nvidia-cuda-nvrtc-cu12` | 12.9.86 |\n"
"| `nvidia-cuda-runtime-cu12` | 12.9.79 |\n"
"| `nvidia-cufft-cu12` | 11.4.1.4 |\n"
"| `nvidia-curand-cu12` | 10.3.10.19 |\n"
"| `nvidia-cusolver-cu12` | 11.7.5.82 |\n"
"| `nvidia-cusparse-cu12` | 12.5.10.65 |\n"
"| `nvidia-nvjitlink-cu12` | 12.9.86 |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `nvidia-*-cu12` versions can change when the environment is rebuilt. "
"Code that depends on an exact CUDA library version might need updates after "
"a new release.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Request a package {#request-a-package}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If other users would also need a package, [request it on "
"GitHub](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-"
"serverless/issues/new?template=pip_dependency_request.yaml). An accepted "
"package is added to the environment in a later release. Until then, or for a"
" private package, [add it as a wheel](#add-your-own-packages).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: issue #2017 removes the request template, but the public PR "
"Qiskit/qiskit-serverless#2651 keeps it. Confirm that the link remains. */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add your own packages {#add-your-own-packages}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To use a package that is not installed, collect its wheel files on your "
"computer, upload them to the workflow's file storage, and install them at "
"the start of the workflow. You upload them again only when they change.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Build wheels {#build-wheels}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The job installs wheels without an internet connection, so each wheel must "
"work with Python 3.12 on Linux (x86_64). Collect the wheels in one folder:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`Local terminal`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With `--platform` and `--python-version`, `pip download` gets wheels for the"
" job's platform, even when you run it on macOS or Windows. It also downloads"
" the package's dependencies, such as `python-dateutil`, `six`, and `tzdata` "
"for `pendulum`. Because the job installs each wheel without its "
"dependencies, upload a wheel for every dependency that the environment "
"lacks, and delete the other wheels from the folder.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A pure-Python wheel (`py3-none-any.whl`) works on any platform. If a package"
" with compiled code has no Linux x86_64 wheel on PyPI, build one on Linux, "
"for example in a `python:3.12` container. Keep the original file names, "
"because `pip` reads the package name, version, and platform from them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Upload wheels {#upload-wheels}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the wheels from your local notebook with `add_wheels()`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each path can be a file name or a glob pattern, and `add_wheels()` returns "
"the names of the uploaded wheels. If a pattern matches no files, or matches "
"a file that is not a `.whl` file, `add_wheels()` raises a "
"`QiskitServerlessException`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Upload the workflow before you add wheels, because the wheels are stored "
"with it. They go to a `wheels` folder in the workflow's [file "
"storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows), separate from your "
"other files.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Replace or remove wheels {#replace-or-remove-wheels}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To see the wheels that are uploaded to a workflow, call `list_wheels()`. To "
"remove wheels, pass their file names to `remove_wheels()`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To upgrade a package, remove the old wheel, and then add the new one. A new "
"version has a different file name, so if you keep the old wheel, "
"`install_uploaded_wheels()` installs both versions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install wheels in your workflow {#install-wheels-in-your-workflow}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Edit your workflow code to call `install_uploaded_wheels()` before it "
"imports the packages:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`install_uploaded_wheels()` installs every wheel in the `wheels` folder. If "
"the workflow has no wheels, the call does nothing. The wheels are installed "
"again in every run, so a large set of wheels adds to the start time of each "
"job.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Best practice: bring only missing packages {#best-practice-bring-only-"
"missing-packages}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a best practice, upload wheels only for the packages that the environment"
" lacks. A wheel for an installed package, such as `numpy`, installs a second"
" copy, and the code that imports it can get either copy. Errors from a "
"mismatch appear only when the job runs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before you upload, check your requirements with `dependency_report()` from "
"your local notebook:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: dependency_report() compares with dependencies_versions() only, so it reports numpy, qiskit, qiskit-ibm-runtime, and qiskit-serverless as \"bring\", although the environment includes them (still true in qiskit-serverless 0.38.0). Fix the report, or keep the note after the list. */}\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The report gives each requirement one of the following statuses:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`baked`: The environment already provides the package. Do not upload a wheel"
" for it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`bring`: The environment lacks the package. Upload a wheel for it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`clash`: The environment provides a different version. Change the version "
"that your code requires, or rebuild your package for the installed "
"version.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The report checks only the supported packages, so it shows `qiskit`, "
"`qiskit-ibm-runtime`, `qiskit-serverless`, and `numpy` as `bring`. The "
"environment includes them, so do not upload wheels for them. The report "
"shows `clash` only for an exact `==` version. It shows a range, such as "
"`>=0.10`, as `baked`. The report does not upload any files.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot dependencies {#troubleshoot-dependencies}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `pip install` fails inside the workflow. | The job cannot reach the internet. [Upload a wheel](#add-your-own-packages) instead. |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` for a package that you uploaded. | The workflow imports the package before it calls `install_uploaded_wheels()`. |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` for a dependency of a package that you uploaded. | Wheels are installed without their dependencies. Upload a wheel for the missing dependency. |\n"
"| The error says that a wheel `is not a supported wheel on this platform`. | The wheel is for another operating system or Python version. Get a wheel for Python 3.12 on Linux x86_64. |\n"
"| `install_uploaded_wheels()` fails with `ResolutionImpossible`. | The `wheels` folder has two versions of the same package. Remove the old wheel with [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| A CUDA package, such as `cupy`, fails on a GPU compute profile after you upload wheels. | A wheel replaced one of the [CUDA packages](#packages-on-gpu-compute-profiles) that the environment provides. Remove that wheel with [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| An installed package, such as `numpy`, fails after you upload wheels. | A wheel installed a second copy of a package that the environment provides. Remove that wheel with [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
msgstr ""
